        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-322777"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p><a href="https://odysseylogistics.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=63c0150c50b9490924dcf316" class="user-hover" rel="63c0150c50b9490924dcf316" data-account-id="63c0150c50b9490924dcf316" accountid="63c0150c50b9490924dcf316" rel="noreferrer">Adam Shingle</a> <a href="https://odysseylogistics.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A5d1c7dfc-e6eb-4f7a-a39b-cab8bf56d4d6" class="user-hover" rel="712020:5d1c7dfc-e6eb-4f7a-a39b-cab8bf56d4d6" data-account-id="712020:5d1c7dfc-e6eb-4f7a-a39b-cab8bf56d4d6" accountid="712020:5d1c7dfc-e6eb-4f7a-a39b-cab8bf56d4d6" rel="noreferrer">Laurie Blumsack</a> : This story has been reviewed by <a href="https://odysseylogistics.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A03aa3c7b-ea4a-46af-9e43-b286e289791e" class="user-hover" rel="712020:03aa3c7b-ea4a-46af-9e43-b286e289791e" data-account-id="712020:03aa3c7b-ea4a-46af-9e43-b286e289791e" accountid="712020:03aa3c7b-ea4a-46af-9e43-b286e289791e" rel="noreferrer">Dave Schultz</a> . All looks good but I needed some more input from Dave, I have put all those queiries as part of this email, and also I have dropped an email to Dave for the same. So, I have put this story as blocked.</p>

<p><a href="https://odysseylogistics.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A03aa3c7b-ea4a-46af-9e43-b286e289791e" class="user-hover" rel="712020:03aa3c7b-ea4a-46af-9e43-b286e289791e" data-account-id="712020:03aa3c7b-ea4a-46af-9e43-b286e289791e" accountid="712020:03aa3c7b-ea4a-46af-9e43-b286e289791e" rel="noreferrer">Dave Schultz</a> : Please have a look into the email and provide the clarification. The details of the email are as follows:</p>

<p>While refining the story <b>"Provide Secure Accept and Decline Actions for Email Tenders"</b>, I came across a few open questions from our discussion that require clarification before we finalize the requirements.</p>

<p>Could you please help with the following?</p>

<ol>
	<li><b>Tender Response Method</b>
	<ul>
		<li>When a carrier accepts or declines a tender from the secure email tender review page, what should be recorded as the Tender Response Method?</li>
		<li>Should it be recorded as <b>Manual</b>, or should a separate value such as <b>Email</b> be used?</li>
	</ul>
	</li>
	<li><b>Decline Reason Requirement</b>
	<ul>
		<li>When a carrier selects <b>Decline</b>, should a decline reason be mandatory or optional?</li>
		<li>Are there any business rules that determine when a decline reason is required?</li>
	</ul>
	</li>
	<li><b>Decline Reason Values</b>
	<ul>
		<li>What list of decline reason codes/values should be presented to the carrier?</li>
		<li>Is there an existing code table or master data source that we should reference?</li>
	</ul>
	</li>
	<li><b>Proposed Pickup and Delivery Dates</b>
	<ul>
		<li>Should carriers be allowed to propose alternate pickup and/or delivery dates from the tender review page?</li>
		<li>If yes, what are the business rules that determine when date changes are allowed?</li>
		<li>Is this capability required as part of MVP?</li>
		<li>Does the current system support this behavior today?</li>
	</ul>
	</li>
</ol>

        </td></tr>
